    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;14.02</strong> Clinical criteria for the diagnosis of serrated polyposis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "source error",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p><strong>Criterion 1:</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"505\">\r\n<p>&ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;serrated lesions/polyps proximal to the rectum, all being &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mm in size, with &ge;&nbsp;2 being &ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm in size</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"104\">\r\n<p><strong>Criterion 2:</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"505\">\r\n<p>&gt;&nbsp;20 serrated lesions/polyps of any size distributed throughout the large bowel, with &ge;&nbsp;5 being proximal to the rectum</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"609\">\r\n<p>Any histological subtype of serrated lesion/polyp (hyperplastic polyp, sessile serrated lesion without or with dysplasia, traditional serrated adenoma, and unclassified serrated adenoma) is included in the final polyp count. The polyp count is cumulative over multiple colonoscopies.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
